fin(x) → [πreg(g)fin](x) = fin(σ−1(g)x) , g ∈ G , (1.15)
where σ is a representation of G that dictates the transformation of the image. In other
words, the color channels are not mixed by the spatial transformations. However, for image
classification the identification of images should be completely independent of how they are
transformed. For this reason we expect the network N (fin) to be invariant under G,
N (πreg(g)fin) = N (fin) , g ∈ G . (1.16)
On the other hand, when doing semantic segmentation we are effectively classifying each
