in this class are tensor product nonlinearities [38, 23] which compute the tensor product of
two Fourier components of the input feature map. They yield a feature map transforming in
the tensor product representation which is then decomposed into irreducible representations.
To eschew the large tensors in this process, [24, 30] introduce various refinements of this basic
idea.


